553 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (We ended up choosing the claw gripper because it was the only design that consistently met the scoring requirements when we tested all three mechanisms in cad and real life out of cardboard. The drag box and servo launcher looked fast at first, but once we simulated them, both showed major accuracy issues. The drag box needs perfect alignment to push the cube into the triangle, and even small turns made the cube drift. The launcher had the same problem but worse: even a tiny angle error caused the cube to miss the triangle completely.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [42]
>>
endobj
554 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E <>
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [43]
>>
endobj
555 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Overall, even though the drag and launcher were faster in collection, the claw was the only one that gave reliable scoring, proper placement, and stacking ability. That consistency and the additional points for stacking is why we chose the claw as our final mechanism.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [44]
>>
endobj
