/E (We thought about more aggressive ideas: camera-based color + bearing tracking, AprilTag localization, and fully vision-driven autonomous pickup/stacking, but rejected them for this season due to latency, lighting sensitivity, extra laptop dependencies and the risk of catastrophic failure in match conditions. Instead, we deliberately constrained the assist to local, high-confidence behaviors \(distance-based approach and scripted pickup\) while planning future prototypes \(dual ToF angle sensing, vision-assisted targeting, richer fuzzy/PID fields\) for the autonomous challenge and stacking tasks once the current assistive layer is fully battle-validated.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [31 32]
>>
