1010 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (These simultaneous sessions created a bridge between theory and practice. Students learned how code translates into movement and how mechanical constraints influence programming decisions. By dividing responsibilities between software and hardware domains, our team delivered a complete, interconnected view of robotics that helped students understand not only how a robot works, but why it behaves the way it does. This dual-club model became the foundation of our school outreach strategy.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [14]
>>
