1013 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The Technologia Club sessions focused on giving students practical exposure to programming as it applies to real robots. We introduced them to JavaScript fundamentals, simple algorithmic thinking, and basic automation concepts so they could understand how logic structures influence robotic behaviour. We then transitioned into MicroPython inside the Arduino IDE 2, allowing students to write short scripts that controlled LEDs, activated servos, and manipulated basic motor functions.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
1014 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Students practiced writing small drills such as timed motion sequences, sensor-triggered responses, and variable-speed routines. This hands-on coding experience helped them see immediate results on a robot-like platform, reinforcing the connection between software and real-world systems. The goal was not only to teach programming but to build confidence and curiosity, empowering students to explore more advanced robotics concepts on their own.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [17]
>>
